AB  - This chapter includes clinical cases, background, evidence-based practical management options, preventive measures, key-point summaries of endometrial development in ART and answers to questions patients ask. Various endometrial characteristics, such as endometrial thickness, endometrial pattern and subendometrial blood flow have been described as prognostic factors. A detailed patient history may reveal any of the detrimental events which could have damaged the endometrial lining. 3D ultrasound with power Doppler angiography has the advantage of assessing simultaneously endometrial volume and endometrial blood flow. Occasionally, in a fresh IVF cycle there may not be adequate follicular development which may lead to a thin endometrium. Oral estrogen is often used to thicken the endometrium in preparation for a frozen embryo transfer cycle as it plays an essential role in endometrial regeneration and growth.
